# Repos deliberately excluded from devbrain-repo-audit's monitoring and from
# devbrain's execution scope. Each line is a decision you made, with its reason —
# adding a line here is a deliberate act, same as in devbrain-projects.allow.
#
# A repo listed here stops appearing in the digest even if it's not in .allow and
# not cloned locally. NOT listing it here (and not being in .allow) is what makes
# devbrain-repo-audit flag it as "repo-sin-clasificar" (unclassified).
#
# Format: name  # reason
#
# machine-config (or whatever you name your devbrain checkout) and any repo that
# holds this system's own code/config should always be excluded here — letting
# devbrain touch its own security allowlist unattended means a nightly loop could
# modify its own permissions with nobody watching. See docs/wiki-example/lessons/
# for the general shape of that lesson.
#
# Example (edit to match your own devbrain checkout's directory name):
# machine-config  # this repo's own code — interactive-only, never nightly
